// Darwin half of the `bit_rt_host_target` port (#1635): the LAST ABI symbol
// only `runtime/root.zig` still defined. `runtime/root/darwin`'s provider
// answers 2 — `BuildTarget.Aarch64Macos` in compiler/build.bit, whose ordinals
// are 0 `x86_64-linux`, 1 `aarch64-linux`, 2 `aarch64-macos`.
//
// WHY A RUNNING PROOF AND NOT JUST `rootpins`. The pin gate proves the symbol is
// defined and free of the post-#1583 self-cycle; it cannot see the VALUE. An
// off-by-one here is silent and expensive: `hostBuildTarget()` is the default
// `bit build`/`bit run` target when `--target` is absent, so a wrong ordinal
// makes the self-hosted compiler emit for the wrong machine and nothing else
// complains. So this program compares the ported provider against the ordinal
// itself, and against a SECOND, independent source of the same fact.
//
// THE INDEPENDENT ORACLE, and its expiry date. `hostTarget()` is a seed
// `prim_rt_fns` entry that lowers to a call to `bit_rt_host_target` — TODAY the
// Zig in `runtime/root.zig`, derived from Zig's own compile-time
// `builtin.target`. The ported provider is pinned under the placeholder name
// `bit_rt_root_host_target`, so the two are DIFFERENT symbols from DIFFERENT
// toolchains and their agreement is real evidence. Once #1583 drops the `_root`
// infix and #1584 builds the archive from Bit, they become the SAME symbol and
// `seedAgrees` turns tautological — at which point the literal comparison
// `ordinal == 2` below is what still carries the test. Both are asserted for
// exactly that reason; do not drop the literal as redundant.
//
// `darwin-only`: this imports `runtime/root/darwin`, whose siblings declare
// libSystem `extern function`s that a Linux target rejects (E0078) even
// uncalled. `../roothostlinux` is the mirror.

import { rtHostTarget } from "../../../runtime/root/darwin"

fn main() {
  let ordinal = rtHostTarget()

  // The provider's own answer, and its agreement with the still-Zig primitive.
  let seedAgrees = ordinal == hostTarget()

  print("roothostdarwin ordinal=${ordinal} isAarch64Macos=${ordinal == 2} seedAgrees=${seedAgrees}\n")
}
